    "last_assistant_text": "`cont->size` comes from `H5F_DECODE_LENGTH(f, p, cont->size)` — directly from the file data! If we craft a continuation message with a very small `size` (like 1, 2, or 3), then `udata->size` will be 1/2/3, the cache will allocate a buffer of that size, read that many bytes, and then call `H5O__cache_chk_verify_chksum(image, 1|2|3, udata)` which calls `H5F_get_checksums(image, 1|2|3, ...)` — and BOOM, heap-buffer-overflow READ 4!\n\nNow I need to craft a v2 object header with a continuation message that has a very small `size` value. Let me build this:",
